  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 92b2c8003586277498a007ee213cc22b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Log - impostor
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FloppyData
  diskName: Log - impostor
  logTitle: Unauthorized File Access
  author: Capt. Michael Hayes
  shipName: 008-Anqa
  dateRecorded: '[Mission timestamp TBD]'
  logText: 'I''m documenting this because it''s happened twice now, and I''d rather
    have a record of it than keep second-guessing myself.

    Yesterday morning
    I noticed that several personal files had been opened while I was asleep. Nothing
    important. Family photographs, some old correspondence, a few recordings from
    home.

    I dug into the access history. According to the computer, I was the
    one who opened them.

    I wasn''t.

    I assumed it was a timestamp error
    or some kind of indexing problem. I''ve had stranger issues with this machine.

    Then
    I got back from the surface today and found my things had been moved.

    My
    jacket was hanging beside the cabin door. I left it folded on my bunk. One of
    the storage drawers was open, and I''m certain I''d closed it before leaving.

    I
    checked the ship''s access records. No unusual entries. No indication that anyone
    boarded while I was away.

    Obviously, nobody did. There''s nobody else out
    here.

    I''ve checked the compartments twice. There''s nothing missing, nothing
    damaged, and no sign of a break-in.

    I don''t know what to make of it.

    Maybe
    I''m more tired than I thought. Maybe I''ve started doing things without remembering
    them.

    But I know I didn''t open those files.

    And I know where I left
    my jacket.

'
